course: dictionary
lesson: 5665
title: The litre
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A litre is a unit for measuring how much liquid there is, or how much space something takes up inside. That space is called volume. «A litre is 1000 millilitres (ml).» So a litre is a big amount, and a millilitre is a very small one.
explain: Look at the clues in «An adult elephant can hold about 8 litres of water in its trunk.» Litres tell us how much water fits, not how heavy it is. Eight litres is a lot of water.
explain: Litres are used for measuring milk, juice and fuel. «A dairy cow can give 25 to 30 litres a day» tells us how much milk a cow makes. In science, we measure liquids with a measuring jug or cylinder.
fact: A litre is 1000 millilitres, so 1 litre = 1000 ml.
fact: To change litres into millilitres, multiply by 1000: 2 litres is 2000 ml.
fact: A litre can also mean an amount that fills that much, like a litre of milk.
fact: In the USA the spelling is liter, and many cars there measure fuel in gallons.
fact: «Most flushes use several litres» of water when you flush a toilet.
exercise: «A litre is 1000 millilitres (ml).» How many millilitres are in 2 litres? | 20 | *2000 | 1000 | 200
exercise: «A dairy cow can give 25 to 30 litres a day.» What does litres measure in this sentence? | Time | *Liquid, such as milk | Weight of the cow | Length
exercise: Maya says a litre is a unit for weight, like kilograms. Is she right? | Yes, a litre measures how heavy something is | Yes, but only for milk | *No, a litre measures how much liquid or space there is | No, a litre measures time
test: How many millilitres are in 1 litre? | 10 | 10000 | 100 | *1000
test: «An adult elephant can hold about 8 litres of water in its trunk.» What does this sentence tell us about litres? | Litres measure how long the elephant is | Litres measure how many elephants there are | *Litres measure how much liquid fits | Litres measure speed
exam: A cup holds 250 ml. How many cups can you fill from a 1 litre bottle? | 2 | 5 | *4 | 3
